# No silent data or credential changes

- Never change passwords, API keys, env secrets, admin users, or other credentials unless the user explicitly asks.
- Never mutate production/local live data (DB rows, uploads, seeded content) for “testing convenience” without prior agreement.
- Prefer read-only verification, fixtures, or disposable test DB. If a write is required to verify, ask first and state exactly what will change.
- If a previous mistake locked or altered credentials, restore only with user confirmation — except when the user explicitly asks to fix a lockout/block they just reported.
